{"challenge_axes":[],"difficulty":3,"generation_seed":20261009,"generator_version":"1.0.0","oracle_version":"independent-1.0.0","producer_agent_id":"/root/relational_critic_producer","producer_role":"producer","record_hash":"db025db593e1158b246d78caafa3f4c5239ba93bdcd668fbeaabec8933c048ca","rendered_input":"Executable task contract:\nJSON scalar values in this task are null, boolean, integer (excluding boolean), or string. No floating point or coercion is used. Scalar equality is type-sensitive. Malformed tasks are outside the valid-task domain.\nInput: `alphabet` is a nonempty list of distinct strings, `slots` a positive integer, `constraints` a list, `candidates` a list of `{candidate_id:string,assignment:[alphabet_symbols]}` with distinct IDs and exactly slots entries, and `min_distance` a nonnegative integer. Constraints are exactly `{kind:\"equal\",positions:[i,j]}`, `{kind:\"different\",positions:[i,j]}`, `{kind:\"allowed\",position:i,values:[alphabet_symbols]}`, or `{kind:\"count\",value:alphabet_symbol,min:integer,max:integer}`. Positions are zero-based in range. All constraints must hold: equal/different compare the indicated entries, allowed requires membership (empty values is impossible), and count requires min<=number_of_matching_entries<=max. Enumerate every length-slots assignment over alphabet; feasible_count counts assignments meeting all constraints. For each candidate in input order, original_valid reports feasibility. Choose its repaired assignment by minimizing (Hamming distance from original assignment, full assignment lexicographic sequence) among feasible assignments. Hamming distance counts unequal positions. If no assignment is feasible, repaired and edit_distance are null. Otherwise edit_distance is the minimal Hamming distance and repaired is the canonical chosen assignment. For diversity, sort candidates with non-null repairs by (edit_distance,candidate_id) ascending. Greedily accept a candidate exactly when its repaired assignment's Ham